From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2000
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix: demote internal TBU no-op path to DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER

In drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/hw/dp_dev.c, demote the
"Connect mmu without internal TBU!" / "Disconnect mmu without
internal TBU!" messages from DRM_WARN to DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER.

The code path is intentionally a no-op when the CIX Linlon-DP block
is configured without an internal Translation Buffer Unit (which is
the case on the Sky1 firmware variant we ship).  WARN-on-no-op is
noisy without being actionable.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  70120-drm-cix-demote-internal-tbu-noop-logs.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds
  70120-drm-cix-demote-internal-tbu-noop-logs.patch]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/hw/dp_dev.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/hw/dp_dev.c
index 31301c960..14968d9c4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/hw/dp_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/hw/dp_dev.c
@@ -595,7 +595,7 @@ static int dp_connect_iommu(struct linlondp_dev *mdev)
 	int i, ret;
 
 	if (!dp->integrates_tbu) {
-		DRM_WARN("Connect mmu without internal TBU!\n");
+		DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER("No internal TBU; skipping display MMU connect\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
 	linlondp_write32_mask(reg, BLK_CONTROL, 0x7, TBU_CONNECT_MODE);
@@ -625,7 +625,7 @@ static int dp_disconnect_iommu(struct linlondp_dev *mdev)
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!dp->integrates_tbu) {
-		DRM_WARN("Disconnect mmu without internal TBU!\n");
+		DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER("No internal TBU; skipping display MMU disconnect\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
 
